summary:
SWE-agent 1.0 + Claude 3.7 set a new SoTA on SWE-Bench Full (2k issues).
The improvement on the issues that are not also in the Lite/Verified subsets is much higher than the gain for the Lite/Verified subsets. Evaluating only on Lite/Verified doesn’t tell the whole story! --&gt;
📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Gk4fa_FWIAAvwgb.png

@18jeffreyma 's coverage driven testgen approach was pivotal in generating the high coverage test suites we have in ProgramBench!
📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HHkmiP-a4AAeXL-.jpg
📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HHkmrRUacAAMsSU.png
Quoting @18jeffreyma
using mini-swe-agent to scalably construct this benchmark was one of my favorite parts of building this: compositionally building longer horizon tasks leveraging the improving capabilities of current coding agents supervised by simple objective signals (like code coverage)

